Subject: CP-T2.2: required hyper-raft API compatibility
Why: The shared Hyper-Raft pin advances to fixed4d72 while preserving the ahead Focal f805 base. Explicit Flushed disk mode, Decimated acknowledgements and disabled FEC preserve existing policy. The bounded replica reports its own declared allowance and holds, forwards stopped/disk liveness facts to the existing Replica, and surfaces disk-mode mismatch; advisory transport progress does not release stream ownership.

